PolicyManagerConsumeTest
├── When no attempt was ever recorded
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and ask no method.
├── When the attempt was cancelled
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt and ask no method.
├── When a new setup ended the attempt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When a clear ended the attempt
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When another address calls
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt naming the caller and leave the attempt waiting.
├── When the call names another action
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt naming that action.
├── When the attempt id is not the live one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId carrying both ids and ask no method.
├── When the attempt was judged under another nonce
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt carrying both nonces and ask no method.
├── When the wait is not over
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WaitNotOver carrying the time and the end of the wait and ask no method.
├── When one second of the wait is left
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WaitNotOver.
├── When the wait is zero
│   └── It should consume the attempt in the block it opened.
├── When the wait is any length
│   └── It should refuse one second before its end and consume at its end.
├── When the block timestamp is past the uint48 width
│   └── It should revert with SafeCastOverflowedUintDowncast carrying the width and the timestamp.
├── When the payload hash is not the committed one
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongPayload carrying both hashes and ask no method.
├── When no attempt waits and every other check fails
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
├── When the id the nonce the wait and the payload all fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongAttemptId.
├── When the nonce the wait and the payload all fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_StaleAttempt.
├── When the wait and the payload both fail
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WaitNotOver.
├── When the payload fails and a used method reports a stop
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_WrongPayload and ask no method.
├── When the first used method reports a stop
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodVetoedSpend naming it and leave the attempt waiting.
├── When only the second used method reports a stop
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodVetoedSpend naming it.
├── When every used method reports a stop
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_MethodVetoedSpend naming the first.
├── When a method the attempt did not use reports a stop
│   └── It should consume the attempt without calling that method.
├── When the pause read reverts
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read reverts with true
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns nothing
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns less than a word
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns a word other than true
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns true and more
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the pause read returns a huge answer
│   └── It should consume the attempt on a gas budget that copying the answer would exhaust.
├── When the pause read writes state
│   └── It should consume the attempt and leave the method's storage untouched.
├── When a used method has no code
│   └── It should consume the attempt.
├── When the attempt ignores stops
│   └── It should consume the attempt without calling any method.
├── When a stop lifts before the spend
│   └── It should consume the attempt at the end of its wait.
├── When the wait is over and no used method vetoes
│   ├── It should set the attempt to Consumed and keep the rest of its record.
│   ├── It should emit AttemptConsumed alone.
│   ├── It should ask each used method once by a static call and call nothing else.
│   └── It should leave the setup and the attempt counter unchanged.
├── When the same spend is sent twice
│   └── It should revert with PolicyManager_NoActiveAttempt.
└── When an attempt opens after the spend
    └── It should open the next id.
